public with sharing class RecordAccessService {

    private static final Integer CHUNK_SIZE = 100;

    /**
     * Returns the subset of recordIds that the running user has edit access to,
     * as determined by the UserRecordAccess object.
     *
     * @param recordIds  Up to 2,000 record IDs (may span multiple objects).
     * @return A set of IDs the user can edit. Never null; empty if input is null/empty
     *         or no records are editable.
     */
    public static Set<Id> editableIds(Set<Id> recordIds) {
        Set<Id> editable = new Set<Id>();
        if (recordIds == null || recordIds.isEmpty()) {
            return editable;
        }

        List<Id> idList = new List<Id>(recordIds);
        Id userId = UserInfo.getUserId();

        // UserRecordAccess has a hard limit of 200 records per query.
        // We chunk the IN-clause to 100 IDs so that even if a record has
        // up to 2 access-source rows, each query stays at or under 200 rows.
        // For 2,000 IDs this yields at most 20 queries — within the budget.
        for (Integer i = 0; i < idList.size(); i += CHUNK_SIZE) {
            Integer upper = (i + CHUNK_SIZE < idList.size()) ? i + CHUNK_SIZE : idList.size();
            List<Id> chunk = new List<Id>();
            for (Integer j = i; j < upper; j++) {
                chunk.add(idList[j]);
            }

            List<UserRecordAccess> accessRows = [
                SELECT RecordId
                FROM UserRecordAccess
                WHERE UserId = :userId
                  AND RecordId IN :chunk
                  AND HasEditAccess = true
            ];

            for (UserRecordAccess access : accessRows) {
                editable.add(access.RecordId);
            }
        }

        return editable;
    }
}
```

**Fix summary:**

| # | Error | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | `UserRecordAccess` has a **200-record-per-query** limit; querying 2 000 IDs at once returns far more than 200 rows | Reduced chunk size from 1 000 to **100** IDs per query. 2 000 / 100 = **20 queries**, exactly within the budget, and each query returns ≤ 200 rows (safe even if a record has up to 2 access-source rows). |
| 2 | `end` is a reserved identifier (previous round) | Renamed to `upper` (already fixed). |
| 3 | `List.sublist` doesn't exist in Apex (previous round) | Manual loop to build each chunk (already fixed). |
| 4 | `UserRecordAccess` requires `UserId = :singleId` (previous round) | `UserId = :userId` present (already fixed). |

